TEMPORARY INSTRUMENTATION for scripts/tests/subagent-load/ — NOT APPLIED, and deliberately kept out of
src/ because it monkey-patches better-sqlite3 and must never ship. It is preserved here only so the
decisive measurements can be reproduced without re-deriving them.

    git apply scripts/tests/subagent-load/loadtrace.patch && npm run build
    node scripts/tests/subagent-load/matrix.mjs
    git apply -R scripts/tests/subagent-load/loadtrace.patch && npm run build

Applied, it adds three per-process signals to every run: sql-<pid>.tsv (every better-sqlite3 call that
blocked its thread >50 ms, plus every SQLITE_BUSY throw, with SQL and call site), lag-<pid>.tsv
(event-loop delay percentiles every 250 ms) and canary-<pid>.tsv (a trivial daemon INSERT every 100 ms
whose duration is essentially pure write-lock wait). Without it the harness still records health.tsv,
cpu.tsv and wal.tsv, which is enough to see a stall but not to attribute one.

